3,Musical aspects of Austronesian culture - Academia.eduStream euraxx | Listen to Austronesian traditional music ...Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and ...,https://www.academia.edu/4175401/Musical_aspects_of_Austronesian_culture,"Musical forms correlate with the expansion of Austronesian culture in the Indo-Pacific. Polyphonic choral singing shows significant similarities between Taiwan and South China. The Jews' harp, developed in South China, spread to Taiwan and the Austronesian region. Listen to Austronesian traditional music, a playlist curated by euraxx on desktop and mobile. Conventionally divided into Taiwan, the Malay Archipelago, Oceania, and Madagascar, Austronesia comprises a huge number of diverse cultural traditions, bound together by their affiliation with the Austronesian expansion and language family, and a shared ancestry.",N’kep,Austronesian
